UPDATE companies SET description='LA Fashion Source operates from Los Angeles, California. The company was founded by Shalcy Robins, who brings 16 years of experience across wholesale, vertical retail, and corporate operations in the fashion industry. Robins established the business to help apparel companies manage manufacturing and sourcing more efficiently.

The firm provides end-to-end apparel services spanning design, development, and production. Its design phase covers tech packs, pattern cards, pattern making, sample making, and specialty cuts. In production, it handles grading, cut-and-sew manufacturing, screen printing, sublimation, embroidery, and garment finishing such as trimming, pressing, folding, labeling, bagging, and packaging. LA Fashion Source also sources fabrics, trims, and hardware, leveraging domestic and international vendor relationships, including factories in Mexico and China for high-volume cut-and-sew orders.

Clients include fashion brands and apparel companies producing categories such as athleisure, women’s dresses, denim, and other soft goods. The company serves both business-to-business and business-to-consumer operations, offering support from product costing and logistics to quality assurance and import management.

Robins created LA Fashion Source to remove the operational headaches of manufacturing and sourcing, promising a single point of contact that can handle any project scale while maintaining quality and cost targets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut & Sew", "Fabric, Trim, and Hardware Sourcing", "Garment Finishing (trimming, pressing, folding, labeling, bagging, packaging)", "Design Services (tech packs, pattern cards, specialty cuts)", "Pattern Making", "Sample Making", "Grading", "Screen Printing", "Sublimation", "Embroidery", "Production Scheduling", "Quality Assurance", "Logistics and Import Support"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Athleisure", "Women''s Dresses", "Denim", "Soft Goods"], "materials": ["Fabrics", "Trims", "Hardware"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Domestic and international vendor relationships for fabrics, trims, and hardware", "Overseas production partnerships in Mexico and China for high-volume cut-and-sew", "In-house team of pattern makers, sample sewers, cutters, screen printers, and embroidery specialists", "Full-service offering from design through retail-ready finishing", "Focus on taking the headache out of manufacturing and sourcing for fashion companies"], "facts_used": ["Location: Los Angeles, California -> db", "Founder: Shalcy Robins -> /about", "Founder experience: 16 years in fashion industry -> /about", "Company experience: over 12 years in industry -> /about", "Services: design, pattern making, sample making, grading, cut & sew, screen printing, sublimation, embroidery, garment finishing, sourcing -> /about and /", "Overseas factory relationships: Mexico and China -> /about", "Industries served: apparel, athleisure, women''s dresses, denim, soft goods -> / and /about", "Aim: help fashion companies run business with ease, take headache out of manufacturing and sourcing -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LA Fashion Source is a sourcing and apparel manufacturing company that was developed with the aim of helping fashion companies run their business with ease.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='la-fashion-source' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LAPCO Factory Outlet Store operates in Morgan City, Louisiana, as the direct retail outlet for Lapco-branded flame-resistant workwear. The company sells factory seconds—garments with minor imperfections or sizing deviations that fall short of first-quality standards—alongside discontinued styles from the main retail line. No founding year or ownership details are disclosed in public sources.

The outlet stocks a range of FR apparel including jeans, shirts, jackets, and steel-toe boots. Products feature fabrics such as 10-ounce cotton denim, 7-ounce UltraSoft AC, 5-ounce Tecasafe® One inherent blends, and 6-ounce Tecasafe® Plus knits. Items are sold individually at marked-down prices; the website lists dozens of SKUs with regular and sale pricing. Facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not published.

The store serves industrial workers and safety managers seeking cost-effective FR protection. Typical end users include oilfield, electrical utility, and construction personnel who accept cosmetic flaws in exchange for lower cost. The outlet explicitly markets to “anyone looking for a great deal or who doesn''t mind fixing a minor flaw.”

