UPDATE companies SET description='LEV Manufacturing operates from Cookeville, Tennessee, with an additional engineering and prototyping hub in Florida. The company serves as the U.S.-based production, engineering, and logistics arm of the Life EV Group of Companies, a structure that emerged from the group''s earlier work manufacturing ProdecoTech electric bicycles (2010–2018) and developing the Life EV brand from 2019 onward. After acquiring the Serial 1 e-bike line from Harley-Davidson in 2023, the group formalized LEV Manufacturing in 2024 to handle contract assembly, private-label builds, and FTZ-based production for both its own brands and partner brands.

The company provides end-to-end services for light electric vehicles: design and engineering of platforms, battery packs, and IoT systems; contract assembly and quality control under a Foreign Trade Zone (FTZ) for duty-free production; and warehousing with drop-ship fulfillment. Its Florida site handles engineering, prototyping, and logistics, while a 100,000-square-foot Tennessee facility is planned for multi-line assembly and FTZ operations. LEV Manufacturing supports private-label and OEM programs with minimum order quantities of 100–500 units, offering a build-as-you-sell model and $10 million in product liability coverage.

LEV Manufacturing serves the light electric vehicle sector, including e-bike and scooter brands. Its portfolio includes the ProdecoTech line produced under OE manufacturing from 2010 to 2018, the Life EV brand developed since 2019, and the Serial 1 e-bike line acquired from Harley-Davidson in 2023. The company also works with external partner brands seeking contract assembly, private-label production, or FTZ-based import advantages.

LEV Manufacturing emphasizes its FTZ-enabled duty-free assembly, low minimum orders, and domestic component storage as key differentiators. The build-as-you-sell model aims to reduce inventory risk for brands, while U.S.-based warranty support and drop-ship fulfillment shorten delivery times. The planned Tennessee facility is designed to scale multi-line assembly for GEN4 platforms with integrated IoT and battery pack production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and engineering", "Product development", "Platform development", "Battery system design", "IoT integration", "Contract assembly", "Quality control", "FTZ processing", "Warehousing and domestic storage", "Drop-ship fulfillment", "Private label manufacturing", "OEM manufacturing", "Licensing", "Contract builds"], "industries": ["Light electric vehicles", "Electric bicycles", "EV components"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FTZ duty-free assembly", "Low MOQs (100\u2013500 units)", "Domestic component storage with free options", "Drop-ship fulfillment", "Build-as-you-sell inventory model"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Cookeville, Tennessee -> db", "Florida HQ for engineering, prototyping, storage, shipping -> /", "Planned Tennessee facility 100K+ sq ft, multi-line assembly, FTZ -> /", "Timeline: ProdecoTech USA OE manufacturing 2010-2018, Life EV development 2019-present, Serial 1 acquisition 2023, LEV MFG expansion 2024-2026 -> /", "Capabilities: Design & Engineering, Manufacturing, Warehousing & Logistics, Private Label/OEM -> /", "MOQs 100-500, fast turnaround, licensing, contract builds -> /", "Why Choose LEV: FTZ duty-free, domestic storage, free storage, USA warranty, drop-ship, build-as-you-sell, $10M liability -> /", "Innovation: GEN4 platforms, IoT integration, battery pack assembly -> /", "Part of Life EV Group of Companies -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LEV Manufacturing is the U.S.-based production, engineering, and logistics arm of the Life EV Group of Companies, supporting both our brands and partner brands. Private Label/OEM Low MOQs, fast turnaround, licensing, contract builds", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "100\u2013500 units", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lev-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LG Billet USA operates from Chandler, Arizona, where it designs and machines billet aluminum accessories for Chevrolet and GMC trucks. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or the names of its founders.

The product line focuses on interior and exterior trim pieces—shift levers, door handles, hood releases, grab handles, climate knobs, and battery mounts—for Chevy/GMC C/K trucks from 1960 through 1998, Silverado/Sierra models from 1999 to 2013, S10 pickups (1982–2004), and Camaros (1967–1992). Parts are CNC-machined from 6061 aluminum, then assembled and packaged in-house. Finishes include a raw machined look, black anodizing, and black powder coating. The catalog lists dozens of distinct part numbers, each offered in multiple finish options.

LG Billet USA sells directly to retail customers through its e-commerce site, which offers free shipping on orders over $150 and international delivery. A “Become A Dealer” link indicates a wholesale channel for resellers.

