UPDATE companies SET description='LKQ Auto Parts of Lincoln operates at 3450 North 35th Circle in Lincoln, Nebraska. The location is part of LKQ Corporation, a national network of automotive salvage and recycled parts facilities. The page does not disclose the founding date of this specific site, nor does it identify individual founders or ownership structure beyond the corporate parent.

The facility functions as a salvage yard and parts distributor, offering used auto body parts, recycled components, remanufactured engines, rebuilt transmissions, and a full line of paint, body, and equipment supplies. Inventory includes radiators, wheels, tires, abrasives, detailing products, and refinish and coating materials. Customers can purchase on-site, arrange local delivery, or have parts shipped via common carriers with tracking. No facility square footage, employee count, or annual volume figures are published for this location.

Testimonials on the site reference individual vehicle owners in Lincoln who obtained painted-to-match body panels and mechanical components. The company also lists "Replacement Automotive Labels" and "Keystone Automotive - Lincoln" among its served categories, indicating a mix of trade and consumer channels.

LKQ emphasizes that the bulk of its salvage-yard inventory consists of original equipment manufacturer (OEM) parts installed by the vehicle maker. It differentiates itself by providing shipment tracking on delivered orders, a 30-day return window with core-charge refunds, and access to extended warranty options through the corporate website.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Salvage parts harvesting", "Parts recycling", "Engine remanufacturing", "Transmission rebuilding", "Paint and body equipment supply", "Refinish and coating supply", "Auto body repair support", "Detailing services", "Radiator supply", "Wheel and tire sales", "Automotive label replacement"], "industries": ["Replacement Automotive Labels", "Keystone Automotive - Lincoln", "Automotive collision repair", "Automotive mechanical repair", "Auto parts distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["OEM parts sourced from manufacturer-installed salvage vehicles", "Ships auto body and mechanical parts with carrier tracking", "Remanufactured engines and rebuilt transmissions in stock", "Full paint, body, and equipment (PBE) product line", "30-day return policy with core charge refunds"], "facts_used": ["Location address and business name -> /", "Part categories and services listed -> /", "Shipping and tracking policy -> /", "Return policy details -> /", "OEM parts claim -> /", "Testimonials from customers -> /", "Corporate affiliation LKQ Corporation -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Salvage and Recycled Auto Parts in Lincoln 68504 | LKQ", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lkq-auto-parts-of-lincoln' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LMI Manufacturing operates from a 40,000-square-foot facility in Hartford, Wisconsin. The company was founded in 1960 on a family farm in the Midwest by Lloyd Luedtke, who invented the Luedke Hay Mover/Hay Conditioner to reduce harvest time for local farmers. After decades of agricultural equipment innovation — including a bale thrower patented for Ford Motors — the business transitioned into a full-scale welding and fabrication shop. In 2018, Ryan Konicek purchased the company and invested in facility renovations and expanded capabilities.

Today LMI provides end-to-end metal fabrication for OEMs nationwide. Core processes include 6 kW fiber laser cutting (up to 79" × 158"), offline-programmed press brake forming, manual and robotic welding certified to 1-inch thickness, CNC milling and turning, and turnkey assembly — all under one roof. The shop also runs turret punching, sawing, grinding, roll forming, and tube bending, with finishing and powder coating coordinated through local partners. A team of roughly 35 employees works across robotic welding cells, CNC machining centers, and precision press brakes.

The company serves OEMs in food processing and packaging (stainless-steel trays, molds, washdown-ready weldments), electrical and power distribution (custom enclosures, lugs, welded assemblies), industrial machinery (large welded frames and system components), data centers (server-room cabinets and hardware), material handling and logistics (conveyor supports, lift-system assemblies, brake components), and agriculture (structural weldments for soil-prep and irrigation equipment). Medical and healthcare customers are also noted.

LMI emphasizes in-house control from laser cutting through final assembly, which shortens lead times and improves traceability. The company reports that 80 percent of quotes are returned within 24–48 hours, and it reserves 20 percent of shop capacity for emergency jobs. Certified welds, QA tracking, and ISO 9001:2015 certification support repeatable quality, while real-time shop-floor dashboards enable accurate lead-time commitments. Average production lead time is two to three weeks, with rush options available.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting (6 kW fiber, up to 79\" \u00d7 158\")", "Metal forming (offline-programmed press brake)", "Welding (manual and robotic, certified up to 1\" thick)", "CNC machining (milling and turning)", "Assembly (turnkey subassemblies and component integration)", "Turret punching (58-station)", "Sawing", "Grinding", "Roll forming (8\" roll diameter)", "Tube bending", "Finishing & powder coating (via local partners)", "Sheet metal punching"], "industries": ["Food Processing & Packaging", "Electrical & Power Distribution", "Industrial Machinery", "Data Centers", "Material Handling & Logistics", "Agriculture & Dirt Movement", "Medical & Healthcare"], "materials": ["Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["6 kW fiber laser (79\" \u00d7 158\" bed)", "Robotic welding cells", "CNC machining centers (multiple, travels up to 60\" \u00d7 30\" \u00d7 28\")", "Precision press brakes (28\u2013350 ton, 10\u201312 ft die surface)", "Turret punch press (58 stations, 30 RPM)", "Roll forming machine (8\" roll diameter, 6 ft bed)", "CNC milling machines (spindle up to 12,000 RPM)", "CNC turning centers (spindle bore 3.02\", 7,500 RPM)", "Sawing equipment"], "volume": "Low to mid-volume; prototype to production", "lead_time": "2\u20133 weeks average; rush capacity available (20% reserved)", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0004\" repeatability (laser); \u00b10.005\" (press brake forming)", "built_on": ["80% of quotes returned within 24\u201348 hours", "20% of shop capacity reserved for rush/emergency jobs", "In-house control: laser cutting, forming, welding, machining, and assembly managed start to finish", "Certified welds with QA tracking and production repeatability", "60+ years of industrial fabrication experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1960 on family farm in Midwest by Lloyd Luedtke -> /about-us", "Headquarters Hartford, Wisconsin -> /about-us, /", "Facility 40,000 sq ft -> /about-us, /", "Employee count ~35 -> /about-us", "Ownership: Ryan Konicek purchased in 2018 -> /about-us", "Core capabilities: laser cutting, forming, welding, machining, assembly -> /, /capabilities", "Equipment: 6kW fiber laser (79x158), robotic welding cells, CNC machining centers, press brakes -> /, /capabilities", "Industries served: food processing, electrical, industrial machinery, data centers, material handling, agriculture, medical -> /", "Quote turnaround: 80% under 48 hours -> /, /about-us", "Rush capacity: 20% reserved -> /, /about-us", "Lead time: 2-3 weeks average -> /", "Certification: ISO 9001:2015 -> /, /about-us", "Tolerances: repeatability 0.0004\", press brake \u00b10.005\" -> /capabilities", "Materials: stainless steel mentioned for food processing -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing You Can Count On", "founded_year": "1960", "employee_count": "35", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lmi-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LS ELECTRIC America is headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois. No founding year for the U.S. entity is disclosed, and ownership details such as family or veteran status are not stated in the source material.

The company provides complete low- and medium-voltage power distribution solutions, including transformers, switchgear, switchboards, panelboards, and DC power systems. Its product lineup features the Load Interrupter Switch, Susol UL Smart MCCB, Dead Tank Circuit Breaker, Susol UL ACB, Metal Enclosed Load Interrupter Switchgear, RPP, UL SPD, and Susol UL MCCB (up to 1000 V). Beyond hardware, LS ELECTRIC America runs a Connect Portal for quotes, order tracking, and document management; a Tech Hub with video tutorials and service guides; a Download Center for catalogs and datasheets; and a certified hands-on training program for each product line. The firm emphasizes integrated manufacturing and supply capabilities but does not publish facility size, headcount, or production volumes.

Industries served include data centers, power grid operators, oil and gas, mining, public infrastructure, general industrial, and commercial and residential construction. The company positions its solutions for mission-critical applications such as data centers, manufacturing plants, and commercial infrastructure projects.

LS ELECTRIC America highlights its integrated manufacturing and supply chain, comprehensive warranty coverage across all 50 states, and dedicated engineering and service expertise as key differentiators. Recent press announcements note a VSC-HVDC joint venture with GE Vernova and a European expansion partnership with LS Cable & System, underscoring a focus on next-generation power transmission technology.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Low-voltage power distribution", "Medium-voltage power distribution", "Transformer manufacturing", "Switchgear manufacturing", "Switchboard manufacturing", "Panelboard manufacturing", "DC power systems", "Engineering and design support", "Technical training and certification", "Product selection and configuration tools", "After-sales service and support"], "industries": ["Data Center", "Power Grid", "Oil & Gas", "Mining", "Public Infrastructure", "Industrial", "Commercial & Residential"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Load Interrupter Switch", "Susol UL Smart MCCB", "Dead Tank Circuit Breaker", "Susol UL ACB", "Metal Enclosed Load Interrupter Switchgear", "RPP", "UL SPD", "Susol UL MCCB (up to 1000 V)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated manufacturing and supply capabilities", "Comprehensive warranty coverage across 50 states", "Certified hands-on training by LS ELECTRIC experts", "Connect Portal for quotes, orders, and document management", "Tech Hub with step-by-step video tutorials and service guides"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lincolnshire, Illinois -> db", "Part of LS Electric group with 50+ years experience -> /", "Presence in 107 nations -> /", "Warranty coverage across 50 states -> /", "LV & MV power distribution solutions (transformers, switchgear, switchboards, panelboards, DC power systems) -> /", "Product lines: Load Interrupter Switch, Susol UL Smart MCCB, Dead Tank Circuit Breaker, Susol UL ACB, Metal Enclosed Load Interrupter Switchgear, RPP