UPDATE companies SET description='Lansdale Semiconductor Inc. operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it has spent more than four decades producing mission-critical, high-reliability semiconductors for military and commercial markets. The company is led by President R. Dale Lillard, who has overseen its expansion into aftermarket manufacturing of classic integrated circuits.

The firm manufactures over 3,000 classic IC designs in their original packages, replicating parts originally produced by AMD, Fairchild, Freescale, Harris, Intel, Motorola, National, Philips (Signetics), and Raytheon. Its semiconductor aftermarket program covers life-cycle management, JAN- and SMD-qualified devices, and RoHS/REACH-compliant production, allowing customers to avoid redesigns of legacy systems.

Lansdale serves aerospace and defense, commercial wireless, and telecommunications sectors. Its components support legacy military platforms and commercial infrastructure, with Raytheon having awarded the company a Four-Star Excellence rating. The company also maintains a network of distribution partners for global reach.

The business was built on the premise that obsolescence should not force a redesign. By continuing to fabricate exact replicas of discontinued ICs, Lansdale provides a continuous, cost-effective supply for systems where substitution is not an option, and it actively combats counterfeit parts in the supply chain.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS','REACH']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor aftermarket manufacturing", "IC life-cycle management", "JAN-qualified manufacturing", "SMD-qualified manufacturing", "RoHS compliance", "REACH compliance", "Conflict minerals reporting", "Obsolescence management", "Counterfeit mitigation", "Part marking", "Distribution partner program"], "industries": ["Aerospace and defense", "Commercial wireless", "Telecommunications", "Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufactures over 3,000 classic IC designs in original packaging", "Exact reproductions of parts from AMD, Fairchild, Freescale, Harris, Intel, Motorola, National, Philips/Signetics, and Raytheon", "Life-cycle management program ensures continuous supply without redesign", "JAN- and SMD-qualified military parts", "RoHS and REACH compliant with conflict-minerals reporting"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Manufactures over 3,000 classic IC designs in original package -> home page", "Replicates parts from AMD, Fairchild, Freescale, Harris, Intel, Motorola, National, Philips/Signetics, Raytheon -> home page", "President: R. Dale Lillard -> home page", "Over 40 years manufacturing mission-critical semiconductors -> home page", "Serves aerospace and defense, commercial wireless, telecommunications, military -> home page", "Raytheon awarded Four Stars for Excellence -> home page", "RoHS and REACH compliance -> home page", "JAN & SMD parts listing -> home page", "Life-cycle management program -> home page", "Counterfeit prevention focus -> home page"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Lansdale Semiconductor still manufactures some of the most popular\u2026and timeless commercial wireless, telecommunications, military and aerospace integrated circuits (IC''s) classic designs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lansdale-semiconductor-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Brookings, South Dakota, Larson Manufacturing produces storm doors, retractable screens, and replacement parts for residential entryways. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founder names.

The product line includes the Maximum View storm door series with interchangeable glass and screen panels, retractable screens for doors, windows, and patios, and a range of replacement components such as sweeps, handlesets, and magnetic closers. Manufacturing processes, facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not specified.

Larson serves homeowners directly through its e‑commerce site and retail channels, while also supporting a network of dealers and installation professionals via a dedicated Pro Center program. Its products are used in residential construction, remodeling, and home‑improvement projects.

The company highlights its SureLatch™ magnetic locking technology, which provides an audible click to confirm secure closure, and the Maximum View door design that maximizes natural light. Additional differentiators cited include free U.S. shipping on all storm door orders, expert‑tested installation guides, comprehensive warranties, and a brand portfolio representing over 200 combined years of material‑science expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Storm door manufacturing", "Retractable screen manufacturing", "Replacement parts manufacturing", "Product design and innovation", "Dealer training and support (Pro Center)", "Installation guidance and product literature"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SureLatch\u2122 magnetic locking technology with audible click confirmation", "Maximum View storm door with largest window opening and interchangeable glass/screen panels", "Free U.S. shipping on all storm door orders", "Expert\u2011tested installation guides and comprehensive warranties", "200 combined years of material\u2011science expertise across brand portfolio"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brookings, South Dakota -> db", "Manufactures storm doors, retractable screens, and replacement parts -> /", "Offers SureLatch\u2122 Magnetic Locking Technology -> /", "Provides free U.S. shipping on all storm doors -> /", "Operates Pro Center for dealers and professionals -> /", "Part of brand portfolio including Therma-Tru, Fiberon, Fypon, Solar Innovations -> /", "Copyright 2026 Larson Manufacturing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SHOP Storm Doors Screens Replacement Parts", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='larson-manufacturing' AND approved AN