UPDATE companies SET description='Laser Metal Fabrication operates from Twin Falls, Idaho, in the Magic Valley region. The company was founded by Cort Johnson, who holds a bachelor''s degree in Welding Fabrication Technology from Brigham Young University–Idaho and a master''s in Project Management from Idaho State University. Johnson has lived in Twin Falls for nine years with his family, and his technical expertise and local roots form the basis of the business.

The shop provides precision laser cutting of sheet, plate, and tube — handling material from 24 gauge through 1-inch plate on sheets up to 6 by 12 feet, and tube up to 8 inches by 21 feet. CNC bending covers sheet metal up to 11 feet and tubing up to 24 feet with a 2.5 mm tolerance, supported by a 150-ton, 10-foot press brake. Welding capabilities include SMAW, MIG, TIG, and laser welding, complemented by fully integrated assembly services and 3D modeling and design. The facility runs documented production workflows to support scalable production for both industrial and ornamental applications.

Laser Metal Fabrication serves contractors, manufacturers, and engineering teams across industrial, commercial, and private projects. The company also produces custom home products such as window well covers and vent covers for residential and commercial clients. Its regional footprint spans the Intermountain West, with service areas including Twin Falls, Jerome, Buhl, Burley, and the broader Magic Valley, while nationwide shipping is available for production parts.

The company positions itself as a partner rather than a vendor, emphasizing documented processes for repeatability and quality control from one-off prototypes to full production runs. Its instant CAD estimator allows customers to upload DXF, DWG, STL, STEP, or IGES files for review-ready estimates, and the shop handles secondary services — forming, welding, and assembly — under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser sheet cutting (24 gauge to 1-inch plate)", "Laser tube cutting (up to 8\" x 21 ft)", "CNC bending and forming (sheet up to 11 ft, tube up to 24 ft, 2.5 mm tolerance)", "SMAW welding", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Laser welding", "Assembly services", "3D modeling and design", "Custom fabrication", "Metal fabrication (custom components, enclosures)", "Production workflow management"], "industries": ["Contractors", "Manufacturers", "Engineering teams", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Residential", "Intermountain West regional"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Industrial-grade laser cutting equipment", "150-ton, 10-foot press brake", "CNC tube cutting machine", "CNC bending equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "2.5 mm tolerance on CNC bending", "built_on": ["\"Partner, not vendor\" collaborative approach", "Documented production workflows for repeatability and quality control", "In-house secondary services (forming, welding, assembly) under one roof", "Instant CAD estimator for review-ready quotes", "Nationwide shipping for production parts"], "facts_used": ["Location: Twin Falls, Idaho -> /about-us", "Founder: Cort Johnson -> /about-us", "Founder education: BYU-Idaho (Welding Fabrication Technology), Idaho State University (Project Management) -> /about-us", "Founder residency: 9 years in Twin Falls -> /about-us", "Laser cutting capacity: 24 gauge to 1-inch plate, sheets up to 6x12 ft -> /services", "Laser tube cutting: up to 8\" x 21 ft -> /services", "CNC bending: sheet up to 11 ft, tube up to 24 ft, 2.5 mm tolerance -> /services", "Press brake: 150-ton, 10-foot -> /services", "Welding processes: SMAW, MIG, TIG, laser -> /services", "Assembly services: fully integrated -> /services", "3D modeling & design -> /services", "Documented production workflows -> /services", "Custom home products: window well covers, vent covers -> /", "Service area: Twin Falls, Jerome, Buhl, Burley, Magic Valley, Intermountain West -> /", "Nationwide shipping for production parts -> /", "Instant CAD estimator accepts DXF, DWG, STL, STEP, IGES -> /", "Materials: steel, aluminum, stainless -> /services", "Company positioning: partner not vendor -> /about-us", "Instagram handle: @lasermetalfab -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Serving contractors and manufacturers with sheet, plate and tube cutting, forming, welding, and custom fabrication.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.instagram.com/lasermetalfab/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='laser-metal-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LCL Electronics is based in Baxter, Minnesota. The company is a HUBZone-certified small business that primarily serves the U.S. Department of Defense and all five branches of the U.S. Armed Forces. It holds a CAGE code of 2Y430 and is ITAR registered.

The company provides electronic manufacturing and assembly services, including surface mount technology, wave and reflow soldering, cable and wiring harness assembly, conformal coating, encapsulation potting, and mechanical assembly. Engineering support includes test equipment design and mechanical development using SolidWorks 3D CAD.

LCL Electronics works with defense and aerospace customers, including the U.S. Department of Defense, all five military branches, and Lockheed Martin as an approved supplier. Its NAICS classifications cover relay and industrial control manufacturing and printed circuit assembly.

