UPDATE companies SET description='Lefty Production Co. operates from a suite on West 9th Street in downtown Los Angeles, California. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but its principals describe learning the trade by producing collections in Asia and South America before returning to domestic manufacturing. The team is led by Marta Miller, a former apparel brand owner, and includes pattern makers and sewers with years of industry experience.

The firm functions as a one‑stop development house and contract manufacturer for apparel and accessories. Its service chain covers sourcing and design, pattern making, sample creation, duplicate samples, marking and grading, size testing, laser cutting, cutting and sewing, and final packing. Production runs range from small batches to larger volumes, with low minimums offered to clients who complete development through Lefty. All work is performed in their Los Angeles facility.

Clients span independent designers, established fashion labels, and major retailers. The company cites collaborations with high‑fashion names such as Matthew Williamson, Rosetta Getty, and Christian Siriano, as well as retail accounts including Nordstrom and Neiman Marcus. It has also produced official uniforms for NBC’s Spartan Ultimate Team Challenge and Netflix’s Ultimate Beastmaster, bomber jackets for the Guns N’ Roses Not in This Lifetime Tour, and the prize package for the Project Runway Junior Season 2 winner. Smaller brands like Touch of Terry, Swoveralls, and Major Blue are referenced in testimonials.

Lefty emphasizes a partnership model built on transparent, flat‑rate pricing and discounts tied to the number of designs. The company highlights its commitment to Made‑in‑USA production, decades of collective experience across global supply chains, and active engagement with fashion programs at FIDM, Cal Poly, and Santa Monica College. It was recognized by the Los Angeles Business Journal in 2015.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Apparel design and development", "Fabric and trim sourcing", "Label and branding development", "Pattern making and sample making", "Duplicate sample creation", "Fitting and pattern revision", "Marking and grading", "Size testing", "Laser cutting and cutouts", "Cutting and sewing production", "Packing and finishing", "Consulting and project management", "Web development", "Pre-production coordination"], "industries": ["Men''s Wear", "Women''s Wear", "Children''s Wear", "Swimwear & Bikini", "Athletic Wear", "Lingerie", "Custom & Bridal", "Home Textiles", "Leather & Handbags", "Merch & Accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Batches large and small; low minimums for development clients", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Flat\u2011rate packages to eliminate hourly overruns", "Discounts scaled to the number of designs developed", "Low minimum orders for clients who complete development in\u2011house", "All production performed domestically in Los Angeles", "Decades of collective experience across international and U.S. manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters at 318 West 9th St, Suite #1010, Los Angeles, CA 90015 -> /about", "One-stop shop development house and apparel & accessories manufacturer -> /", "Services: sourcing & design, development, pre-production, production, laser cutting, consulting, web development -> /services", "Worked with Matthew Williamson, Rosetta Getty, Christian Siriano, Nordstrom, Neiman Marcus -> /about", "Produced uniforms for NBC''s Spartan Ultimate