UPDATE companies SET description='Luminus Devices is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California, where it develops and manufactures high-output LED chips and chip-on-board (COB) arrays for a range of lighting and photonics applications. The company operates as a manufacturer of illumination, specialty, and laser diode products, serving global markets through a network of local, regional, and international distributors.

Its product portfolio spans illumination LEDs for retail, hospitality, residential, industrial, outdoor, office, education, museum, and architectural settings, including circadian and human-centric lighting. Specialty lines cover ultraviolet, stage and studio, infrared, projection and display, horticulture, medical and life sciences, and automotive applications. The company also produces lasers and power products such as MOSFETs and Schottky barrier diodes. Recent releases include the SFT-70X high-CRI LED, LUX Pro and Gen6+ COB platforms, CFT-50X series for medical and industrial use, and deep-red SFT-12R and SFT-25R LEDs for stage and horticulture. Online tools such as a horticulture calculator and lumen calculators for COB and mid-power arrays support customer design work.

Collaborations with partners like BluGlass, Current Chemicals, and Cuvée Systems extend its technology reach, including KSF phosphor licensing and joint driver development.

The company emphasizes efficacy, color quality, and real-world performance, citing breakthroughs such as breaking the $0.10 per milliwatt barrier for UVC LEDs and introducing Salud™ COBs with high melanopic-to-photopic ratios for healthy daytime lighting. Proprietary Robusto™ technology enables high-density COB arrays, while KSF phosphor technology enhances color rendering across its product lines.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["LED chip manufacturing", "Chip-on-board (COB) array assembly", "Laser diode manufacturing", "Power semiconductor manufacturing (MOSFETs, Schottky barrier diodes)", "Phosphor technology development (KSF)", "Robusto\u2122 high-density COB technology", "Spectral tuning (RGBW, CCT tunable)", "UV/IR/UVC LED production", "High-CRI LED production", "Horticulture lighting design support", "Lumen calculation tools", "Deep-red LED production", "High-power white LED production", "Mid-power LED production", "Flip-chip mid-power LED production", "Pico-COB production", "Dim-to-warm module development", "Linear module development", "Driver development (through partnership)", "Custom LED packaging"], "industries": ["General Lighting", "Horticulture", "Medical & Life Sciences", "Entertainment (Stage & Studio)", "Automotive", "Industrial", "Projection & Displays", "Ultraviolet Applications", "Infrared Applications", "Human-Centric Lighting", "Retail & Hospitality Lighting", "Architectural & Museum Lighting", "Office & Education Lighting", "Residential Lighting", "Outdoor Lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["High-output LED chips and COB arrays for diverse photonics applications", "Robusto\u2122 technology enabling high-density COB arrays", "KSF phosphor technology for enhanced color rendering", "Salud\u2122 COBs with high melanopic/photopic ratios for human-centric lighting", "Online horticulture and lumen calculators for design support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Sunnyvale, California -> db", "Product description: High-output LED chips and COB arrays for lighting, horticulture, entertainment -> db", "Product categories: Illumination LEDs (retail, hospitality, residential, industrial, outdoor, office, education, museum, architectural, circadian), Specialty LEDs (UV, stage & studio, IR, projection, displays, horticulture, medical, life sciences, industrial, automotive), Lasers, Power Products (MOSFETs, Schottky diodes) -> /", "Global distributor network -> /", "Recent product releases: SFT-70X, LUX Pro, Gen6+ COB, CFT-50X, SFT-12R/25R deep red, MP-3030-120H, RGBW COB, XFM-5050 UVC, etc. -> /", "Online calculators: Horticulture calculator, Lumen calculators for COB and mid-power -> /", "Collaborations: BluGlass, Current Chemicals (KSF phosphor licensing), Cuv\u00e9e Systems (drivers) -> /", "Technologies: Robusto\u2122 high-density COB, KSF phosphor, Salud\u2122 COBs with high melanopic/photopic ratios -> /", "UVC LED cost breakthrough: $0.10 per mW barrier -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "High-output LED chips and COB arrays for lighting, horticulture, entertainment", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='luminus-devices' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Luther''s Welding has operated in Bristol, Rhode Island since 1937. The business began as a small welding shop, incorporated in 1971, and two years later narrowed its focus to marine fabrication.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication, welding, CNC machining, and sheet metal design. Core processes include rolling, sawing, and press brake forming, allowing production of custom marine tanks (fuel, water, holding), OEM and aftermarket marine hardware such as mastheads and chain plates, and sheet metal components for utility trucks. Assembly and leak testing are performed in-house, while finishing services are sourced as needed. The facility handles projects from prototype through medium-volume runs with an emphasis on fast turnaround.

The primary customer base is the marine industry, serving boat builders and owners in the U.S. and Canada. The company also fabricates sheet metal parts for utility trucks and has produced items for various non-marine industrial clients. Tank designs can be supplied by the customer, developed in-house, or reverse engineered from existing components, and are built to American Boat and Yacht Council standards.

Luther''s Welding emphasizes personal service and close customer partnerships, a byproduct of its small-company structure. The staff includes welders with decades of experience and certified qualifications, supported by a machine shop and engineering department each with over 35 years of expertise. The family oversight model is intended to ensure that every product leaving the facility meets the company''s reputation for reliability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Welding", "CNC machining", "Sheet metal design and engineering", "Custom marine tank fabrication", "Rolling", "Sawing", "Press brake forming", "Assembly", "Leak testing", "Finishing services (outsourced)", "Reverse engineering", "Prototype to medium volume production"], "industries": ["Marine", "Marine fuel, water, and holding tanks", "Utility truck", "General industrial"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Steel alloys"], "equipment": ["CNC machining centers", "Press brakes", "Rolling machines", "Saws"], "volume": "Prototype to medium volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with family oversight of every department", "Personal service and close customer partnerships", "In-house design, reverse engineering, and custom tank design", "Assembly and leak testing on all assemblies", "Prototype to medium volume with fast turnaround"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1937 -> /about-us", "Incorporated 1971 -> /about-us", "Marine specialization since 1973 -> /about-us", "Family-owned with family oversight -> /about-us", "Headquarters Bristol, Rhode Island -> db", "Materials: aluminum, steel, steel alloys -> /about-us", "Processes: rolling, sawing, press brake forming -> /", "CNC machining capabilities -> /", "Sheet metal design and engineering -> /", "Custom marine tank fabrication (fuel, water, holding) -> /", "Assembly and leak testing -> /", "Finishing services sourced -> /", "Reverse engineering and in-house design -> /", "Prototype to medium volume production -> /", "Fast turnaround and personal service -> /", "Industries: marine, utility truck, general industrial -> /", "Export to Canada -> /about-us", "ABYC standards for tanks -> products", "Welding certifications (unspecified) -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We began as a small welding shop. In 1971 we became incorporated and two years later we began specializing in the Marine Industry.", "founded_year": "1937", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["Export to Canada"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='luthers-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lutron Electronics was founded in 1961 in Coopersburg, Pennsylvania.

The company produces a range of lighting controls including dimmers, switches, keypads, remotes, and sensors, as well as motorized shades, drapery, and blinds under the Sivoia brand. Its control systems — such as HomeWorks, RadioRA3, Athena, Vive, and myRoom XC — serve residential, commercial, and hospitality projects. Lutron also offers embedded fixture technology for OEM integration. The firm provides commercial project support encompassing design and specification services, installation support, system verification, and technical startup assistance.

Lutron serves architects, builders, electrical contractors, engineers, interior designers, lighting dealers, and facility managers across residential, commercial, and hospitality sectors. Notable projects include the BlackRock headquarters, SOM offices, Hotel Indigo Dubai, Sofitel Rome, Banyan Tree Hotel, The Ritz-Carlton, Taliesin West, and the Stay Bungalow.

