UPDATE companies SET description='MAVIN Furniture operates from Dundee, Ohio, where it produces American-made custom wood furniture. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, nor are its founders named in available materials.

The manufacturer offers a range of residential furniture collections, including a Home Office line, dining tables, the South Port bedroom group, and artful dining chairs. Its products are distributed through a network of more than 700 quality furniture retailers across the United States. Specific facility size, headcount, annual volumes, or part-number counts are not provided.

MAVIN serves the residential furniture market, supplying retailers that cater to homeowners furnishing home offices, dining rooms, and bedrooms. The company''s "Locate a Retailer" feature directs consumers to its nationwide dealer network, which spans coast to coast.

The company emphasizes its American-made origin and a design approach that pairs thoughtful design with flexible customization, allowing customers to personalize pieces through an online design tool. This focus on made-to-order domestic production is presented as its core distinction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wood furniture manufacturing", "Product design and customization", "Retail distribution network management"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home office furniture", "Dining furniture", "Bedroom furniture", "Furniture retail"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made custom wood furniture", "Nationwide distribution through 700+ retail locations", "Online design tool for product customization", "Multiple residential collections (home office, dining, bedroom)"], "facts_used": ["Company name MAVIN Furniture -> db", "Headquarters Dundee, Ohio -> db", "American Made Custom Wood Furniture -> /", "Home Office Collection -> /", "Dining Tables collection -> /", "South Port Bedroom Group -> /", "Artful Dining Chairs -> /", "700+ quality furniture locations nationwide -> /", "Locate a Retailer feature -> /", "Design Now customization tool -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "American Made Custom Wood Furniture", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mavin-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MBC Food Machinery Corporation is based in Hackensack, New Jersey, and has been operating since 1965.

The company designs and builds custom high‑production equipment for the frozen‑filled pasta market, including machines that form ravioli, manicotti, cannelloni, stuffed shells, cavatelli, pierogie, stuffed rigatoni and lasagna. All machinery is manufactured at its Hackensack facility using CAD‑driven processes and materials that meet USDA standards, and each unit is tested before shipment. MBC also runs a full‑service machine shop offering CNC machining, CNC turning, welding and fabrication, and it provides machinery rebuilding services for both domestic and imported equipment. In addition, the firm maintains a stock of replacement parts for immediate dispatch and offers plant‑layout consulting to help customers optimize production space.

MBC’s primary customers are frozen‑food manufacturers in the United States, Canada and Europe that produce filled pasta products. The company’s equipment and services are tailored to high‑volume production lines in the frozen pasta segment.

MBC traces its industry leadership to the introduction of the first automatic manicotti‑cannelloni production line nearly 50 years ago. The company emphasizes U.S.‑based manufacturing, rigorous USDA‑compliant construction, quick‑ship replacement parts designed for easy on‑site changeover, and personalized design services for custom applications — factors it says underpin long‑term customer relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and manufacture of custom high\u2011production industrial food production equipment", "Personalized product design services", "Machinery rebuilding services for imported and domestic equipment", "CNC machining", "CNC lathe work", "Welding", "Fabrication of custom parts", "Production facility consulting and design", "Plant layout and equipment placement consulting", "Replacement parts inventory and immediate shipment", "Equipment testing and validation"], "industries": ["Frozen food industry", "Frozen\u2011filled pasta industry", "Food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Ravioli Machine", "Pasta Cooking and Cooling System", "Automatic manicotti\u2011cannelloni production line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All machinery manufactured at Hackensack, NJ facility to strict USDA requirements", "Each piece of equipment thoroughly tested before leaving the facility", "Complete inventory of replacement parts available for immediate shipment", "Product designs allow easy on\u2011site part replacement to reduce downtime", "Personalized product design services for custom applications and special needs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> db", "Headquarters Hackensack, New Jersey -> db", "Manufactures custom high\u2011production food production equipment for frozen filled pasta -> /about", "Specializes in ravioli, manicotti, cannelloni, stuffed shells, cavatelli, pierogie, stuffed rigatoni, lasagna -> /", "All machinery built in US to strict USDA requirements -> /about", "Uses CAD tools for design -> /about", "Each equipment tested before shipment -> /about", "Offers personalized product design services -> /about", "Maintains replacement parts inventory for immediate shipment -> /about", "Machinery rebuilding services for imported and domestic equipment -> /services", "Full\u2011service machine shop: CNC machining, CNC lathe, welding, fabrication -> /services", "Production facility consulting and design -> /services", "Customers in United States, Canada, Europe -> /about", "First automatic manicotti\u2011cannelloni production line introduced nearly 50 years ago -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1965 MBC Food Machinery Corp. has been a leader in the design and manufacture of custom high-production industrial food production equipment for the frozen-filled pasta industry.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mbc-food-machinery-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mid-Continent Custom Electronics (MCCE), operating as MCC Electronics, is headquartered in Lee''s Summit, Missouri, in the Kansas City metropolitan area. The company was founded in 1972 and has served customers globally from its domestic base for over five decades. In 2012, Mark Dohnalek acquired Pivot International, the global design, engineering, and manufacturing firm that owns MCCE as a subsidiary. Pivot International maintains offices in the United Kingdom and Hong Kong, with additional manufacturing plants in Kansas City and Asia, giving MCCE access to global resources while retaining U.S. production.

MCCE provides single-source original design manufacturing (ODM) and electronic manufacturing services (EMS) for electronic and electro-mechanical products. Its capabilities span hardware design, circuit board layout and assembly (both surface-mount and through-hole), embedded software development, mechanical engineering, and industrial design. The domestic facility handles prototyping, low-volume runs, and high-volume production, performing electro-mechanical panel and box assembly, device programming, custom silkscreening, encapsulating, conformal coating, and in-house test fixture construction. All products undergo 100% inspection at the U.S. plant.

The company serves a diverse industrial base, including unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), agricultural equipment such as combines and hay balers, construction machinery like boom lifts, fire and emergency vehicle door systems, airport and corporate intercom control panels, hospital and detention center security systems, livestock and veterinary scales, and isokinetic exercise data logging. Customers range from OEMs needing full product development to those requiring contract assembly or design rescue.

MCCE emphasizes its domestic manufacturing oversight, global supply chain reach through Pivot International, and award-winning design team as key differentiators. The firm positions itself as a partner that can take a concept through to production, reduce costs on legacy products, improve quality, and recover troubled projects.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Original design manufacturing (ODM)", "Electronic manufacturing services (EMS)", "Industrial design", "Mechanical engineering", "Electrical engineering", "Software development", "Circuit board design, layout and assembly", "Surface mount circuit board assembly", "Through-hole circuit board assembly", "Electro-mechanical panel & box assembly", "Device programming (EEPROM, microprocessor)", "Custom silkscreening (aluminum, stainless steel, painted/powder coated metal)", "Encapsulating", "Conformal coating", "Custom test fixture design and build", "Embedded design and development", "Analog and digital measurement", "Data acquisition and control", "Prototyping", "Low-volume production", "High-volume production", "Project management"], "industries": ["Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)", "Agricultural equipment", "Construction equipment", "Fire and emergency vehicles", "Airport systems", "Corporate office systems", "Hospital and healthcare", "Detention center security", "Livestock and veterinary", "Fitness and medical devices", "Industrial equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Surface Mount Assembly Machine"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source design, engineering, and manufacturing", "Domestic facility with 100% product inspection", "Global resources via Pivot International network", "Over 40 years of electronic design and manufacturing experience", "Award-winning design and development capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1972 -> /", "Headquarters in Lee''s Summit, Missouri -> db", "Subsidiary of Pivot International, acquired by Mark Dohnalek in 2012 -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO9001, ISO13485, ISO14001, ULLISTED, ROHS -> db", "Capabilities: ODM, EMS, design, engineering, manufacturing -> /", "Processes: SMT, through-hole, electro-mechanical assembly, device programming, silkscreening, encapsulating, conformal coating, custom test fixtures -> /capabilities", "Industries served: UAV, agricultural, construction, fire/emergency, airports, corporate, hospitals, detention centers, livestock/veterinary, isokinetic exerciser -> /capabilities", "Equipment: Surface Mount Assembly Machine -> /", "Domestic manufacturing with 100% inspection -> /", "Global resources through Pivot International -> /", "Volume: prototype to high-volume -> /", "Award-winning design -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mid-Continent Custom Electronics (MCCE) is an industry leader in the development of custom-designed electronic components, both original design manufacturing (ODM) and electronic manufacturing services (EMS). We have on-site manufacturing facilities to accommodate prototyping, small run production and full production runs.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mcc-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MCM Engineering II, Inc., operating as LS Electric Utah, is based in Enoch, Utah. The company has specialized in custom switchgear manufacturing for more than 25 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. It operates as a subsidiary of a larger parent organization, though the parent company is not named in available materials.

The firm designs and builds medium‑voltage metal‑clad and metal‑enclosed switchgear that meets ANSI C37.20.1, C37.20.2, and C37.20.3/4 standards. Its product range covers NEMA 1 and NEMA 3R lineups, paralleling switchgear, substations, integrated power stations, utility metering equipment, severe‑environment enclosures, sheltered‑aisle walk‑ins, power distribution centers, and low‑voltage (480 V) assemblies. All work is performed in‑house through integrated design, fabrication, wiring, and assembly departments, with each project assigned a dedicated project manager and mechanical designer.

