UPDATE companies SET description='MDS Manufacturing operates from Pacific, Missouri, where it was founded in 2009 as a family-owned business. The company traces its roots back more than 50 years to Marvin D. Skaggs, a plastics industry veteran whose legacy inspired the MDS name. Today, the firm is led by President Dave Skaggs Sr., Vice President Mike Skaggs, Chief Operating Officer Julie Round, Operations Manager Greg Rodermund, and Quality Control Manager Tyler Skaggs.

The shop provides custom plastic injection molding on presses ranging from 85 to 550 tons, liquid silicone rubber (LSR) molding on high-speed equipment up to 150 tons, and injection stretch blow molding (ISBM) to round out a one-stop-shop offering. It also handles assembly and production tooling, with 3-D prototyping samples available to validate designs before committing to mold construction. Mold lead times are quoted at 6–12 weeks depending on complexity and run size.

MDS serves customers across a broad range of industries worldwide, though the company does not list specific sectors on its site. Its capabilities suit any application requiring precision-molded plastic or silicone components, from prototype through production volumes.

The company emphasizes its family-run culture and a “customer-first philosophy” built on collaboration and transparency. It claims to be the only Midwest manufacturer offering high-speed LSR molding up to 150 tons, and it backs that differentiation with decades of hands-on experience passed down from its founder.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Injection Molding", "Liquid Silicone Rubber (LSR) Molding", "Injection Stretch Blow Molding (ISBM)", "Assembly", "Production Tooling", "3-D Prototyping"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Plastic resins", "Liquid Silicone Rubber (LSR)"], "equipment": ["High-speed liquid silicone molding presses (up to 150 tons)", "Injection molding presses (85\u2013550 tons)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6\u201312 weeks for mold tooling", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only Midwest manufacturer offering high-speed LSR molding up to 150 tons", "3-D prototyping samples delivered in 6\u201312 weeks", "Family-owned with over 50 years of plastics industry heritage", "One-stop-shop: injection molding, LSR, ISBM, assembly, and tooling under one roof", "Customer-first philosophy with collaboration and transparency"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 in Pacific, Missouri -> db", "Family-owned business, legacy of Marvin D. Skaggs -> /", "Leadership team: Dave Skaggs Sr., Mike Skaggs, Julie Round, Greg Rodermund, Tyler Skaggs -> /", "Custom injection molding presses 85\u2013550 tons -> /", "LSR molding up to 150 tons, claimed only Midwest provider -> /", "Injection stretch blow molding (ISBM) offered -> /", "Assembly and production tooling services -> /", "3-D prototyping samples, 6\u201312 week mold lead time -> /", "Serves global customers across wide range of industries -> /", "Customer-first philosophy, collaboration, transparency -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture a wide variety of plastic molded parts and products using presses ranging from 85 to 550 tons.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mds-manufacturing-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MHz Electronics, Inc. is based in Phoenix, Arizona. The company has been buying and selling electronic manufacturing equipment, testing tools, and specialty items for over 35 years. In 1997, it moved to its current 68,000-square-foot facility on East Washington Avenue.

The company operates as a distributor and reseller of electronic components, test equipment, and specialty items. Its inventory exceeds 400,000 parts and equipment, housed in a 68,000-square-foot warehouse that has supported the company’s growth since 1997. MHz Electronics also offers a sourcing service for items not in stock and maintains a want list for customers looking to sell equipment.

The company serves buyers of electronic manufacturing equipment, test instruments, and specialty components across the western United States, with a focus on customers needing hard-to-find or obsolete parts.

