UPDATE companies SET description='Maine Adirondack Chairs, LLC operates from Vassalboro, Maine. The business traces its roots to 2012 when founder Rob transitioned from Grapevine Hill Woodworking to the current name after a suggestion from John Shaw. Rob remains involved while Nita now manages the shop and builds products, alongside Kate.

The company handcrafts outdoor furniture exclusively from Eastern White Cedar (Thuja occidentalis), planing and sanding only one face to yield thicker boards and reduce processing time. The small woodworking shop produces Adirondack chairs, rocking chairs, picnic tables, footstools, coffee tables, and campfire stools, with a capacity of roughly 30–40 chairs per week. Chairs are built then broken down into knock-down kits for shipping; smaller items such as footstools and coffee tables ship assembled.

Products serve both residential buyers and commercial settings—the “EZ‑UP” chair is designed for the rigors of commercial use. Customers order directly through the website, and the build‑to‑order model means inventory rarely sits on hand; high spring demand often leads to backorders by April.

The venture began almost by accident, driven by geographic economic pressures. After sparse demand for custom kitchen cabinets, Rob pivoted to Adirondack chairs, with most designs originating from customer requests and ergonomic experiments. The single‑side milling method and exclusive use of local white cedar keep prices reasonable while delivering rot‑resistant, decades‑long durability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted woodworking", "Single-side planing and sanding", "Knock-down kit assembly", "Custom furniture design", "Ergonomic product development", "Outdoor furniture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Residential outdoor furniture", "Commercial outdoor furniture"], "materials": ["Eastern White Cedar (Thuja occidentalis)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "30\u201340 chairs per week", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exclusive use of Eastern White Cedar for all products", "Single-side planing and sanding for thicker boards and lower cost", "Build-to-order production with 30\u201340 chairs weekly capacity", "Chairs shipped as knock-down kits; smaller items ship assembled", "Designs driven by customer requests and ergonomic testing"], "facts_used": ["Vassalboro, Maine location -> /", "2012 founding year -> /", "Founder Rob -> /", "Nita manages shop and builds products -> /", "Exclusive Eastern White Cedar material -> /", "Single-side planing and sanding process -> /", "30\u201340 chairs per week capacity -> /", "Knock-down kit shipping for chairs -> /", "EZ-UP chair for commercial use -> /", "Build-to-order model with spring backorders -> /", "Product designs from customer requests -> /", "Transition from Grapevine Hill Woodworking in 2012 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a small woodworking shop, and we can build 30\u201340 chairs per week.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maine-adirondack-chairs-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The firm was established to advance renewable energy adoption across the state by connecting residents and businesses with community solar programs.

The company provides enrollment assistance and education for community solar programs, helping customers subscribe to local solar farms without installing panels on their own properties. Its customer relations team guides clients through the signup process, which the company says takes about five minutes, and continues to provide support after enrollment. The firm reports assisting hundreds of Mainers in joining state community solar programs.

Clients include both residential and commercial customers. Restaurant groups, nonprofit organizations such as the Maine State Society for the Protection of Animals, and condominium residents who cannot install rooftop panels have all enrolled through the service.

